>> title: Kitchari
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, lentils, indian, vegetarian, one-pot
>> counters: Curry House, One Pot
>> aka: khichdi, khichari, kitcheree, kichadi, moong dal khichdi
>> pairs-with: chapati
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min
>> washing-up: the saucepan, a sieve to rinse the rice and dal in
>> keeps: 3 days — it sets solid overnight and loosens with a splash of water; the spicing is gentler by then

>> step: rinse
Rinse @basmati rice{1/2%cup}(100 g) and @split mung dal{1/2%cup}(100 g) together until the water runs clear.

>> step: fry 1 min
Fry @cumin seeds{1%tsp}, @black mustard seeds{1/2%tsp}, and @ginger{1%Tbs}(minced) in @ghee{2%Tbs} in a #saucepan{} for ~{1%min}.

>> step: toast 2 min
Toast @&(~2)rice and dal{} in @&(~1)tempering{} with @ground turmeric{1/2%tsp} and @ground coriander{1%tsp} for ~{2%min}.

>> step: simmer covered 25 min
Simmer @&(~1)pot{} covered over low heat for ~{25%min} with @water{4%cups}(950 mL) and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}.

>> step: finish
Finish @&(~1)kitchari{} with @lemon juice{1%Tbs} and @cilantro{2%Tbs}.
